"Four Minutes" - Argentina 2-1 England, World Cup quarter-final, Estadio Azteca, Mexico City, 22 June 1986: an animated fan retelling for the Foot All FC channel. Comic History Cartoon style (lemo-opuscar).
Unofficial: not made or endorsed by the AFA, The FA, FIFA or any broadcaster. No crests, league or competition marks, broadcast footage or real
likenesses are used; players are generic paper puppets identified by shirt number, the referee is a generic puppet, the trophy is a generic drawn cup.

Puppet art: the part sheets of videos/barca-remontada-short (AI-generated, incl. the referee parts), recoloured into generic kits with tools/kit.py:
  plain blue ('arg', Argentina wore blue that day), plain white with navy shorts ('eng', England).
Narration: Microsoft VibeVoice-Realtime-0.5B, voice "Frank" (MIT licence), AI-generated voice. The quote "a little with the hand of God" is Maradona's own (press conference, 22 June 1986), read by the narrator.
Fonts (SIL Open Font License): IM FELL English SC (Igino Marini), Old Standard TT (Alexey Kryukov), Lilita One (Juan Montoreano).
Instruments (sampled, via lemo-opuscar core/audio/sampler.py): see out/instruments.txt at build time.
Samples (CC0): FreePats project (freepats.zenvoid.org), VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios), Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios)
Foley, crowd and applause: synthesized in mix.py.
Facts: see social/scripts/maradona-1986-hand-and-goal.md (fact sheet with sources).
